[{"source" ":org/Math-Academy" "forms" [{:db/id 17592186105920 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-4a1280d0-096f-55e2-a7c1-562a8ea5c435" "question-8c02d34a-4ad8-562b-8457-9fd6ebf13de4" "question-49006a0c-9d9b-5197-b92e-ebd835d319e8"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-4a1280d0-096f-55e2-a7c1-562a8ea5c435" :question/id #uuid "4a1280d0-096f-55e2-a7c1-562a8ea5c435" :question/math-academy-id "q-67314" :question/problem "The eighth and ninth terms of an arithmetic sequence are $65$ and $73,$ respectively. Determine the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the $n$th term is given by  \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\n$$\n\nso we need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nSince the terms ${a}_{8}=65$ and ${a}_{9}=73$ are consecutive, we can subtract them to find the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{9}-{a}_{8} \\\\  & =73-65 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use one of our known values, say, ${a}_{8}=65,$ to determine the first term of the sequence. Since ${a}_{8}$ is $7$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{8} & ={a}_{1}+7d \\\\ 65 & ={a}_{1}+7\\cdot 8 \\\\ 65 & ={a}_{1}+56 \\\\ 65-56 & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the formula for the $n$th term of this arithmetic sequence is:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =9+(n-1)\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =9+8n-8 \\\\  & =8n+1\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-6768b760-5887-55b4-9496-804fe3857fb7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-6768b760-5887-55b4-9496-804fe3857fb7" :answer-field/id #uuid "6768b760-5887-55b4-9496-804fe3857fb7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0cd36596-380b-5e27-8715-406d44365e01" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7e51f011-8ba0-59f1-9885-8e886cef3b24" "answer-9ffac599-99d7-51d3-b553-edfa79b80d70" "answer-b1009998-8bbf-503b-b636-342553fb7361" "answer-0cd36596-380b-5e27-8715-406d44365e01" "answer-dd1cb4fe-a3f5-557e-a340-1f52b2b46bea"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7e51f011-8ba0-59f1-9885-8e886cef3b24" :answer/id #uuid "7e51f011-8ba0-59f1-9885-8e886cef3b24" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=10n-15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ffac599-99d7-51d3-b553-edfa79b80d70" :answer/id #uuid "9ffac599-99d7-51d3-b553-edfa79b80d70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=5n+25" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b1009998-8bbf-503b-b636-342553fb7361" :answer/id #uuid "b1009998-8bbf-503b-b636-342553fb7361" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=7n+9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0cd36596-380b-5e27-8715-406d44365e01" :answer/id #uuid "0cd36596-380b-5e27-8715-406d44365e01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=8n+1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd1cb4fe-a3f5-557e-a340-1f52b2b46bea" :answer/id #uuid "dd1cb4fe-a3f5-557e-a340-1f52b2b46bea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=9n-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186105921 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-d7637fee-b44e-5ca1-97d4-93d38249c26d"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-d7637fee-b44e-5ca1-97d4-93d38249c26d" :question/id #uuid "d7637fee-b44e-5ca1-97d4-93d38249c26d" :question/math-academy-id "q-101047" :question/problem "An arithmetic sequence has the $2$nd term ${a}_{2}=-6$ and the $9$th term ${a}_{9}=-27.$  Calculate the $12$th term." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the $n$th term is given by \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\n$$\n\n \n\nso we need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$ \n\nTo find the common difference, we can find the total difference between the terms ${a}_{2}=-6$ and ${a}_{9}=-27$ and divide it by the number of jumps, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{9}-{a}_{2}}{9-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-(-6)}{9-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-21}{7} \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use one of our known values, say, ${a}_{2}=-6,$ to determine the first term of the sequence. Since ${a}_{2}$ is $1$ jump after ${a}_{1},$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}+d \\\\ -6 & ={a}_{1}+(-3) \\\\ -6 & ={a}_{1}-3 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-3+(n-1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-3n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can find the $12$th term by substituting $n=12$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12} & =-3(12) \\\\  & =-36\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-84a5e98a-dad5-5287-a15e-430d9e0b8531"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-84a5e98a-dad5-5287-a15e-430d9e0b8531" :answer-field/id #uuid "84a5e98a-dad5-5287-a15e-430d9e0b8531" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3d2ad81c-9f64-5962-9de9-22587a298e8a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-74c81dd1-56de-5ff7-a952-f9e8b5886f6d" "answer-3d2ad81c-9f64-5962-9de9-22587a298e8a" "answer-70997eca-2a85-5b07-a632-3a2abbaaac70" "answer-90f45413-b9f5-562d-b014-a8d470ade225" "answer-7ac26f03-c4ab-57b8-af80-17413a6b5f95"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-74c81dd1-56de-5ff7-a952-f9e8b5886f6d" :answer/id #uuid "74c81dd1-56de-5ff7-a952-f9e8b5886f6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-24" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3d2ad81c-9f64-5962-9de9-22587a298e8a" :answer/id #uuid "3d2ad81c-9f64-5962-9de9-22587a298e8a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-36" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-70997eca-2a85-5b07-a632-3a2abbaaac70" :answer/id #uuid "70997eca-2a85-5b07-a632-3a2abbaaac70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-42" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-90f45413-b9f5-562d-b014-a8d470ade225" :answer/id #uuid "90f45413-b9f5-562d-b014-a8d470ade225" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7ac26f03-c4ab-57b8-af80-17413a6b5f95" :answer/id #uuid "7ac26f03-c4ab-57b8-af80-17413a6b5f95" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "45" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8c02d34a-4ad8-562b-8457-9fd6ebf13de4" :question/id #uuid "8c02d34a-4ad8-562b-8457-9fd6ebf13de4" :question/math-academy-id "q-177690" :question/problem "The $9$th and $10$th terms of an arithmetic sequence are $49$ and $45,$ respectively. Determine the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the $n$th term is given by \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\n$$\n\nso we need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$ \n\nSince the terms ${a}_{9}=49$ and ${a}_{10}=45$ are consecutive, we can subtract them to find the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{10}-{a}_{9} \\\\  & =45-49 \\\\  & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use one of our known values, say, ${a}_{9}=49,$ to determine the first term of the sequence. Since ${a}_{9}$ is $8$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{9} & ={a}_{1}+8d \\\\ 49 & ={a}_{1}+8(-4) \\\\ 49 & ={a}_{1}-32 \\\\ 49+32 & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =81.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term of this arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =81+(n-1)(-4) \\\\  & =81-4n+4 \\\\  & =85-4n.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4d2c864f-a858-5345-a4b8-b85451a19550"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4d2c864f-a858-5345-a4b8-b85451a19550" :answer-field/id #uuid "4d2c864f-a858-5345-a4b8-b85451a19550" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f148c23e-a718-5531-a0c4-1174b3fba592" :answer-field/choices ["answer-c976b982-fbc1-5a12-9f25-15205ef6c9f3" "answer-7104255d-539a-5c5c-a1fb-11f319f0ae2e" "answer-f148c23e-a718-5531-a0c4-1174b3fba592" "answer-ccac4e53-8c71-5b88-9d4d-0e21df30e875" "answer-f1c9c8fe-e798-51ad-a501-82b5c80bac50"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-c976b982-fbc1-5a12-9f25-15205ef6c9f3" :answer/id #uuid "c976b982-fbc1-5a12-9f25-15205ef6c9f3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=73-4n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7104255d-539a-5c5c-a1fb-11f319f0ae2e" :answer/id #uuid "7104255d-539a-5c5c-a1fb-11f319f0ae2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=76-3n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f148c23e-a718-5531-a0c4-1174b3fba592" :answer/id #uuid "f148c23e-a718-5531-a0c4-1174b3fba592" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=85-4n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ccac4e53-8c71-5b88-9d4d-0e21df30e875" :answer/id #uuid "ccac4e53-8c71-5b88-9d4d-0e21df30e875" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=89-5n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f1c9c8fe-e798-51ad-a501-82b5c80bac50" :answer/id #uuid "f1c9c8fe-e798-51ad-a501-82b5c80bac50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=94-5n" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-49006a0c-9d9b-5197-b92e-ebd835d319e8" :question/id #uuid "49006a0c-9d9b-5197-b92e-ebd835d319e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-177697" :question/problem "The $6$th and $7$th terms of an arithmetic sequence are $-37$ and $-43,$ respectively. Determine the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence." :question/worked-solution "The formula for the $n$th term is given by \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\n$$\n\nso we need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nSince the terms ${a}_{6}=-37$ and ${a}_{7}=-43$ are consecutive, we can subtract them to find the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{7}-{a}_{6} \\\\  & =-43-(-37) \\\\  & =-43+37 \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use one of our known values, say, ${a}_{7}=-43,$ to determine the first term of the sequence. Since ${a}_{7}$ is $6$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{7} & ={a}_{1}+6d \\\\ -43 & ={a}_{1}+6(-6) \\\\ -43 & ={a}_{1}-36 \\\\ -43+36 & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term of this arithmetic sequence is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =-7+(n-1)(-6) \\\\  & =-7-6n+6 \\\\  & =-6n-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-e1f7ea83-66ac-59bf-a2b2-ac35df55da76"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-e1f7ea83-66ac-59bf-a2b2-ac35df55da76" :answer-field/id #uuid "e1f7ea83-66ac-59bf-a2b2-ac35df55da76" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-27ec5ff2-6947-518e-b5fe-5c489285580d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-63088e18-5037-574e-ad60-35bc9c871285" "answer-dd99c42f-293b-55c0-b44b-582a2580b93f" "answer-b989b406-0a46-579a-8239-7b038482cf61" "answer-27ec5ff2-6947-518e-b5fe-5c489285580d" "answer-f25f65b7-51ea-50c3-9a44-91ca7555b30c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-63088e18-5037-574e-ad60-35bc9c871285" :answer/id #uuid "63088e18-5037-574e-ad60-35bc9c871285" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-4n-13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dd99c42f-293b-55c0-b44b-582a2580b93f" :answer/id #uuid "dd99c42f-293b-55c0-b44b-582a2580b93f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-5n-13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b989b406-0a46-579a-8239-7b038482cf61" :answer/id #uuid "b989b406-0a46-579a-8239-7b038482cf61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-5n-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27ec5ff2-6947-518e-b5fe-5c489285580d" :answer/id #uuid "27ec5ff2-6947-518e-b5fe-5c489285580d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-6n-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f25f65b7-51ea-50c3-9a44-91ca7555b30c" :answer/id #uuid "f25f65b7-51ea-50c3-9a44-91ca7555b30c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{a}_{n}=-6n-7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "activity-a713bb24-782c-567d-be38-331493e992a1" :activity/id #uuid "a713bb24-782c-567d-be38-331493e992a1" :activity/title "Finding the Nth Term of an Arithmetic Sequence Given Two Terms" :activity/type :activity.type/review :activity/scope 17592186049504 :activity/course 17592186046647 :activity/steps ["step-d1d86871-e295-5e22-83f5-f15193e7a1b7" "step-bd4f70e8-81e3-5e70-b511-8fb6bdcbe14a" "step-a05e6f04-e350-5f85-8ea5-d30f83877d47" "step-896351f2-021f-5ace-bde9-20648346cc20"] :activity/first-step "step-d1d86871-e295-5e22-83f5-f15193e7a1b7" :db/ensure [:activity/validate]} {:db/id "step-d1d86871-e295-5e22-83f5-f15193e7a1b7" :step/id #uuid "d1d86871-e295-5e22-83f5-f15193e7a1b7" :step/content "question-4a1280d0-096f-55e2-a7c1-562a8ea5c435" :step/next "step-bd4f70e8-81e3-5e70-b511-8fb6bdcbe14a" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-bd4f70e8-81e3-5e70-b511-8fb6bdcbe14a" :step/id #uuid "bd4f70e8-81e3-5e70-b511-8fb6bdcbe14a" :step/content "question-d7637fee-b44e-5ca1-97d4-93d38249c26d" :step/next "step-a05e6f04-e350-5f85-8ea5-d30f83877d47" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-a05e6f04-e350-5f85-8ea5-d30f83877d47" :step/id #uuid "a05e6f04-e350-5f85-8ea5-d30f83877d47" :step/content "question-8c02d34a-4ad8-562b-8457-9fd6ebf13de4" :step/next "step-896351f2-021f-5ace-bde9-20648346cc20" :db/ensure [:step/validate]} {:db/id "step-896351f2-021f-5ace-bde9-20648346cc20" :step/id #uuid "896351f2-021f-5ace-bde9-20648346cc20" :step/content "question-49006a0c-9d9b-5197-b92e-ebd835d319e8" :db/ensure [:step/validate]}] "assertions" [["question-4a1280d0-096f-55e2-a7c1-562a8ea5c435" :question/id #uuid "4a1280d0-096f-55e2-a7c1-562a8ea5c435"] ["question-4a1280d0-096f-55e2-a7c1-562a8ea5c435" :question/math-academy-id "q-67314"] ["question-4a1280d0-096f-55e2-a7c1-562a8ea5c435" :question/problem "The eighth and ninth terms of an arithmetic sequence are $65$ and $73,$ respectively. Determine the formula for the $n$th term of the sequence."] ["question-4a1280d0-096f-55e2-a7c1-562a8ea5c435" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the $n$th term is given by  \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\n$$\n\nso we need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$\n\nSince the terms ${a}_{8}=65$ and ${a}_{9}=73$ are consecutive, we can subtract them to find the common difference:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={a}_{9}-{a}_{8} \\\\  & =73-65 \\\\  & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use one of our known values, say, ${a}_{8}=65,$ to determine the first term of the sequence. Since ${a}_{8}$ is $7$ jumps after ${a}_{1},$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{8} & ={a}_{1}+7d \\\\ 65 & ={a}_{1}+7\\cdot 8 \\\\ 65 & ={a}_{1}+56 \\\\ 65-56 & ={a}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{1} & =9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the formula for the $n$th term of this arithmetic sequence is:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & ={a}_{1}+(n-1)d \\\\  & =9+(n-1)\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =9+8n-8 \\\\  & =8n+1\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-4a1280d0-096f-55e2-a7c1-562a8ea5c435" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-6768b760-5887-55b4-9496-804fe3857fb7" :answer-field/id #uuid "6768b760-5887-55b4-9496-804fe3857fb7"] ["answer-7e51f011-8ba0-59f1-9885-8e886cef3b24" :answer/id #uuid "7e51f011-8ba0-59f1-9885-8e886cef3b24"] ["answer-7e51f011-8ba0-59f1-9885-8e886cef3b24" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-7e51f011-8ba0-59f1-9885-8e886cef3b24" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=10n-15"] ["answer-9ffac599-99d7-51d3-b553-edfa79b80d70" :answer/id #uuid "9ffac599-99d7-51d3-b553-edfa79b80d70"] ["answer-9ffac599-99d7-51d3-b553-edfa79b80d70" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9ffac599-99d7-51d3-b553-edfa79b80d70" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=5n+25"] ["answer-b1009998-8bbf-503b-b636-342553fb7361" :answer/id #uuid "b1009998-8bbf-503b-b636-342553fb7361"] ["answer-b1009998-8bbf-503b-b636-342553fb7361" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-b1009998-8bbf-503b-b636-342553fb7361" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=7n+9"] ["answer-0cd36596-380b-5e27-8715-406d44365e01" :answer/id #uuid "0cd36596-380b-5e27-8715-406d44365e01"] ["answer-0cd36596-380b-5e27-8715-406d44365e01" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0cd36596-380b-5e27-8715-406d44365e01" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=8n+1"] ["answer-dd1cb4fe-a3f5-557e-a340-1f52b2b46bea" :answer/id #uuid "dd1cb4fe-a3f5-557e-a340-1f52b2b46bea"] ["answer-dd1cb4fe-a3f5-557e-a340-1f52b2b46bea" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-dd1cb4fe-a3f5-557e-a340-1f52b2b46bea" :answer/value "{a}_{n}=9n-7"] ["answer-field-6768b760-5887-55b4-9496-804fe3857fb7" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-6768b760-5887-55b4-9496-804fe3857fb7" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-6768b760-5887-55b4-9496-804fe3857fb7" :answer-field/correct "answer-0cd36596-380b-5e27-8715-406d44365e01"] ["answer-field-6768b760-5887-55b4-9496-804fe3857fb7" :answer-field/choices "answer-7e51f011-8ba0-59f1-9885-8e886cef3b24"] ["answer-field-6768b760-5887-55b4-9496-804fe3857fb7" :answer-field/choices "answer-9ffac599-99d7-51d3-b553-edfa79b80d70"] ["answer-field-6768b760-5887-55b4-9496-804fe3857fb7" :answer-field/choices "answer-b1009998-8bbf-503b-b636-342553fb7361"] ["answer-field-6768b760-5887-55b4-9496-804fe3857fb7" :answer-field/choices "answer-0cd36596-380b-5e27-8715-406d44365e01"] ["answer-field-6768b760-5887-55b4-9496-804fe3857fb7" :answer-field/choices "answer-dd1cb4fe-a3f5-557e-a340-1f52b2b46bea"] ["question-4a1280d0-096f-55e2-a7c1-562a8ea5c435" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-6768b760-5887-55b4-9496-804fe3857fb7"] [17592186105920 :knowledge-point/questions "question-4a1280d0-096f-55e2-a7c1-562a8ea5c435"] ["question-d7637fee-b44e-5ca1-97d4-93d38249c26d" :question/id #uuid "d7637fee-b44e-5ca1-97d4-93d38249c26d"] ["question-d7637fee-b44e-5ca1-97d4-93d38249c26d" :question/math-academy-id "q-101047"] ["question-d7637fee-b44e-5ca1-97d4-93d38249c26d" :question/problem "An arithmetic sequence has the $2$nd term ${a}_{2}=-6$ and the $9$th term ${a}_{9}=-27.$  Calculate the $12$th term."] ["question-d7637fee-b44e-5ca1-97d4-93d38249c26d" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the $n$th term is given by \n\n$$\n{a}_{n}={a}_{1}+(n-1)d,\n$$\n\n \n\nso we need to figure out the first term ${a}_{1}$ and the common difference $d.$ \n\nTo find the common difference, we can find the total difference between the terms ${a}_{2}=-6$ and ${a}_{9}=-27$ and divide it by the number of jumps, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\frac{{a}_{9}-{a}_{2}}{9-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-27-(-6)}{9-2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-21}{7} \\\\  & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use one of our known values, say, ${a}_{2}=-6,$ to determine the first term of the sequence. Since ${a}_{2}$ is $1$ jump after ${a}_{1},$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{2} & ={a}_{1}+d \\\\ -6 & ={a}_{1}+(-3) \\\\ -6 & ={a}_{1}-3 \\\\ {a}_{1} & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the formula for the $n$th term is:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{n} & =-3+(n-1)\\cdot (-3) \\\\  & =-3n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can find the $12$th term by substituting $n=12$ into the above:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{12} & =-3(12) \\\\  & =-36\\end{aligned}\n$$"] ["question-d7637fee-b44e-5ca1-97d4-93d38249c26d" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate] ["answer-field-84a5e98a-dad5-5287-a15e-430d9e0b8531" :answer-field/id #uuid "84a5e98a-dad5-5287-a15e-430d9e0b8531"] ["answer-74c81dd1-56de-5ff7-a952-f9e8b5886f6d" :answer/id #uuid "74c81dd1-56de-5ff7-a952-f9e8b5886f6d"] ["answer-74c81dd1-56de-5ff7-a952-f9e8b5886f6d" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-74c81dd1-56de-5ff7-a952-f9e8b5886f6d" :answer/value "-24"] ["answer-3d2ad81c-9f64-5962-9de9-22587a298e8a" :answer/id #uuid "3d2ad81c-9f64-5962-9de9-22587a298e8a"] ["answer-3d2ad81c-9f64-5962-9de9-22587a298e